        "role": "user",
        "content": "{\"context\":[{\"id\":\"c1\",\"text\":\"Other non-operating income (expense), net | (321) | | (1) | % | (98) | | — | % | (68) | | (1) | % | (559) | | (1) | % | (90) | | — | % |\"},{\"id\":\"c2\",\"text\":\"Income tax (provision) benefit | (4,978) | | (12) | % | (2,371) | | (10) | % | (235) | | (3) | % | (8,178) | | (10) | % | (695) | | (3) | % |\"},{\"id\":\"c3\",\"text\":\"Equity in net income (loss) of equity method investees | 9 | | — | % | (4) | | — | % | 7 | | — | % | 13 | | — | % | 10 | | — | % |\"},{\"id\":\"c4\",\"text\":\"Net income | $ | 28,243 | | 68 | % | $ | 13,785 | | 58 | % | $ | 1,885 | | 20 | % | $ | 47,268 | | 60 | % | $ | 5,338 | | 20 | % |\"}],\"filing\":\"MU 10-Q\",\"section\":\"Part I Item 2\",\"sentences\":[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Consolidated Results\",\"text\":\"Total Revenue: Total revenue for the third quarter and first nine months of 2026 was impacted by the factors described in the section titled “Industry Conditions—Memory and Storage Demand” above.\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Consolidated Results\",\"text\":\"Total revenue for the third quarter of 2026 increased 74% as compared to the second quarter of 2026, primarily due to increases in sales of both DRAM and NAND products.\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Consolidated Results\",\"text\":\"Sales of DRAM products increased 67%, primarily due to a low-60% range increase in average selling prices and a low-single-digit percentage range increase in bit shipments.\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Consolidated Results\",\"text\":\"Sales of NAND products increased 99%, primarily due to a mid-80% range increase in average selling prices and a mid-single-digit percentage range increase in bit shipments.\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Consolidated Results\",\"text\":\"Total revenue for the third quarter of 2026 increased 346% as compared to the third quarter of 2025, primarily due to increases in sales of both DRAM and NAND products.\"},{\"id\":\"s6\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Consolidated Results\",\"text\":\"Sales of DRAM products increased 343%, primarily due to a low-260% range increase in average selling prices and a low-20% range increase in bit shipments.\"},{\"id\":\"s7\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Consolidated Results\",\"text\":\"Sales of NAND products increased 361%, primarily due to a mid-310% increase in average selling prices and a low-double-digit increase in bit shipments.\"},{\"id\":\"s8\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Consolidated Results\",\"text\":\"Total revenue for the first nine months of 2026 increased 203% as compared to the first nine months of 2025, primarily due to increases in sales of both DRAM and NAND products.\"},{\"id\":\"s9\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Consolidated Results\",\"text\":\"Sales of DRAM products increased 211%, primarily due to an approximate 140% increase in average selling prices and an approximate 30% increase in bit shipments.\"},{\"id\":\"s10\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Consolidated Results\",\"text\":\"Sales of NAND products increased 183%, primarily due to an approximate 130% increase in average selling prices and a low-20% range increase in bit shipments.\"},{\"id\":\"s11\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Consolidated Results\",\"text\":\"Consolidated Gross Margin: Our consolidated gross margin has been impacted by the factors described in the section titled “Industry Conditions—Memory and Storage Demand.”\"},{\"id\":\"s12\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Consolidated Results\",\"text\":\"Our consolidated gross margin percentage increased to 85% for the third quarter of 2026 from 74% for the second quarter of 2026 as a result of improvements in margins for both DRAM and NAND products.\"},{\"id\":\"s13\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Consolidated Results\",\"text\":\"Margins improved primarily due to increases in average selling prices and also benefited from continued strong execution and favorable mix.\"},{\"id\":\"s14\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Consolidated Results\",\"text\":\"Our consolidated gross margin percentage improved to 85% for the third quarter of 2026 from 38% for the third quarter of 2025 and improved to 77% for the first nine months of 2026 from 38% for the first nine months of 2025.\"},{\"id\":\"s15\",\"section_path\":\"Part I Item 2 > Consolidated Results\",\"text\":\"Improvements in our consolidated gross margins for the third quarter and first nine months of 2026 as compared to corresponding periods of 2025 were due to improvements in margins for both DRAM and NAND products.\"}]}"
